-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/48ddae05-98a1-44e6-9e9b-ddace6a528f5
-- title:
--   Expanding one valid prefix and retaining exactly its positive child indices
-- statement:
--   Write $S,\Omega,\Delta$ for machine space, word magnitude, and depth limits. Let finite labeled integer inputs $A,B,C$, with maps $a,b,c$, induce raw representations $I$ at integer parameters $p,\delta$. Fix $w=(x,\ell,q)$, where $\ell\in\{-1,0,1\}$, satisfying $x\in A$ and $M\mid a(x)\bmod p+\ell p+\delta-\operatorname{key}(q)$, and a valid prefix $P$ of length $k<J$. Its children $P_i$ append each $h$-element subset of the next $2h$-element output row, so $G=\binom{2h}h$ children are enumerated. Here $M$ is the global block modulus.
--
--   Assume exact source transforms and the complete sorted suffix catalog for level $k+1$. Its query parameters satisfy $t\le r_0+1$, $b\le r_0$, $r_0-t\le b$, where $r_0=2h(J-k-1)$. All retained data precede the ordered child-mask, left-mask, right-mask, count, selection, and query-scratch regions. The stated scratch and word bounds hold, $S\le\Omega$, and $d+1024hJ+15\le\Delta$.
--
--   With $c_i=\#\{u\in I:\operatorname{wanted}(u)=w,\operatorname{word}(u)|_{k+1}=P_i\}$, the routine retains
--   $$[c_i]_{i<G},\qquad [\,i<G:c_i>0\,],\qquad r=\#\{i<G:c_i>0\},$$
--   as well as the enumerated child masks and both child-prefix mask arrays. It preserves memory before the child region and meets the stated child-construction plus level-query budget.
--
--   This performs one verified expansion of the reporting frontier.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingCatalogExpand.lean#L41-L170

